---
---

<section id="about">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal>About</p>
    <h2 class="section-title" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
      The full picture
    </h2>
    <div class="section-divider" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1"></div>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-text" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
        <p>
          I'm a software developer who arrived here through a path most
          resumes don't follow. Before writing TypeScript, I was diagnosing
          vehicles, managing operations teams, building computers from
          components, and figuring out what was wrong when something stopped
          working. That hands-on, systems-level instinct didn't go away when I
          moved into software — it just found a larger surface area.
        </p>
        <p>
          Professionally, I spent four years at MarketVision Research building
          and maintaining custom survey applications in Perl, JavaScript, and
          HTML — owning the full lifecycle from client requirements through
          deployment and post-launch support. I shipped interactive ECharts
          dashboards for non-technical stakeholders, co-developed a VS Code
          extension that automated repetitive workflows across the team, and
          learned what it actually means to maintain production software under
          real pressure.
        </p>
        <p>
          Independently, I designed and built
          <strong>dw-portfolio-platform</strong> — the system powering this
          page. It's a production-grade pnpm + Turborepo monorepo with a
          Next.js app, tRPC API, Drizzle ORM, AI agents backed by
          Anthropic's Claude, eight parallel CI/CD jobs in GitHub Actions, and
          all cloud infrastructure provisioned through Terraform. I built it
          to demonstrate the kind of work I can do end-to-end, and to have
          something worth showing when I walk into an interview.
        </p>
        <p>
          I hold two associate degrees — Computer Information Systems and
          Accounting — and I've consistently been the person in any room who
          figures out how things actually work, not just how they're
          supposed to work.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="about-stats" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="3">
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-value">4+</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Years professional development</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-value">25+</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Packages in flagship monorepo</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-value">8</span>
          <span class="stat-label">Parallel CI/CD jobs shipped</span>
        </div>
        <div class="stat-card">
          <span class="stat-value">3.75</span>
          <span class="stat-label">GPA — Computer Information Systems</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 260px;
    gap: 3rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .about-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1.1rem;
  }

  .about-text p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .about-text strong {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .about-stats {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1rem;
    position: sticky;
    top: 80px;
  }

  .stat-card {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    transition: border-color var(--transition), box-shadow var(--transition);
  }

  .stat-card:hover {
    border-color: var(--border-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }

  .stat-value {
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    color: var(--accent);
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .stat-label {
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .about-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .about-stats {
      position: static;
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>